WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.086
With Rails I18n, views call t,

2
00:00:04.086 --> 00:00:06.767
and someone writes each
locale's YAML file.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.983
Rails I18n does its part well,

4
00:00:09.983 --> 00:00:11.932
with lazy lookup and fallbacks.

5
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.622
General Translation
produces the translations,

6
00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:17.781
and keeps them current
as English changes.

7
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.077
Keep English working files,

8
00:00:21.077 --> 00:00:22.946
and point the gt config at them.

9
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:28.735
Then npx gt translate and a short
export write the Rails catalogs

10
00:00:28.735 --> 00:00:29.721
in CI.

11
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.426
A Glossary keeps terms consistent,

12
00:00:32.426 --> 00:00:35.072
and your team reviews
translations in the Dashboard.

13
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.343
Your team now ships
Spanish with each release.
